# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code's own directory. None of it is site content: settings.local.json
# carries an absolute path from whoever's machine wrote it, launch.json is a
# local dev-server port, and worktrees/ holds whole checkouts. All of it is
# written without being asked, and lands exactly where `git add -A` sweeps.
.claude/

# Another tool's copy of the account pin that .claude/settings.local.json already
# carries, written here without being asked. Same absolute path from whoever's
# machine wrote it, same sweep by `git add -A`, and a repo this public has no use
# for either copy.
.codex/

# A byte-identical copy of CLAUDE.md that tooling writes without being asked. Two files saying
# the same thing drift; if the AGENTS.md convention is wanted here it should replace CLAUDE.md
# rather than sit beside it.
AGENTS.md
